{"schema_version": "1", "exit_code": 0, "command_completed": true, "effect_verification": "not_asserted", "output": "usage: footwork drag-points [-h]\n                            [--mode {background_only,foreground_permitted,exclusive_desktop}]\n                            [--owner OWNER] [--app NAME] [--duration SECONDS]\n                            [--record FILE]\n                            x0 y0 x1 y1\n\nMove the real pointer to X0 Y0 with no button, press, drag to X1 Y1 and\nrelease. Global screen points, origin top left, both in the application named\nwith --app. Prints one JSON object. Exit 0: released at the end point. 4:\nnothing posted. 5: the pointer was moved and the button never pressed. 6:\npressed, and released otherwise than asked (it says where and why). 8:\npressed, and the button cannot be said to be up; the desktop stays claimed.\n\npositional arguments:\n  x0\n  y0\n  x1\n  y1\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --mode {background_only,foreground_permitted,exclusive_desktop}\n                        must be exclusive_desktop: the command moves the real\n                        pointer and holds its button\n  --owner OWNER         who the desktop is claimed for in the coordination\n                        registry (default: this process)\n  --app NAME            required: the application both points are in. It is\n                        claimed with the desktop, and the drag is refused\n                        unless a hit test at each end finds it\n  --duration SECONDS    how long the drag's motion takes, press hold and\n                        settle apart (default: the planner's, about 0.6 s for\n                        a short drag); not shorter than that, at most 30\n  --record FILE         append the drag's pointer_gesture/1 record to FILE\n", "diagnostics": "", "data": null}
